WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.400
He had it, he still couldn’t&nbsp;
believe that he had it.&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.680
Very few professional thieves managed to steal&nbsp;
something so valuable right from under the nose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.240
of the SCP Foundation, and even fewer lived to&nbsp;
tell anyone about it. Kasdan gripped the bag in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:22.640
one hand, holding on so tightly his knuckles felt&nbsp;
like they might split. He was drenched in nervous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.920
sweat, the clamminess of his palms leaving&nbsp;
an imprint on the material of the duffel bag.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.840
Its precious contents moved around loosely; every&nbsp;
time it jostled and knocked against him, Kasdan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:40.560
had to fight the urge to unzip the bag, just to&nbsp;
remind himself this was all actually happening.&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:46.880
But he resisted, he knew the mask wanted not&nbsp;
only to be seen but to be heard as well. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:52.400
earpiece his client had provided was doing its&nbsp;
job, keeping the whispers at bay, dampening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.800
the telepathic aura enough to ensure that Kasdan&nbsp;
retained control over his own faculties. The bag,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.240
he’d been told, would also hopefully dampen&nbsp;
the powers of the mask’s corrosive fluid.&nbsp;

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:09.040
He’d been prepped extensively for this job,&nbsp;
more than any other in his long and storied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:15.040
criminal career. It had taken months of planning,&nbsp;
staking out the home of a Foundation researcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.400
stealing his access card, and slipping into&nbsp;
the heavily-guarded facility undetected.&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.480
As if that hadn’t been hard enough, he&nbsp;
then had to find the right containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:30.400
cell containing what he’d been hired to steal.&nbsp;
Just like any heist, the timing was everything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.440
He had to make sure he was there on the exact day&nbsp;
the glass container housing his target was due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.840
be replaced thanks to corrosion damage, having&nbsp;
been gradually melted and worn away over time.&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:48.000
At an intensely precise moment on precisely&nbsp;
the right day, Kasdan had to enter the cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.800
and sedate not only the research staff that&nbsp;
had come to swap out the glass container&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.960
but the armed guards posted outside, too. Then,&nbsp;
it was just a case of slipping on the specialized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.560
gloves he’d been issued, grabbing the mask, and&nbsp;
stashing it in the bag with protective lining to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.680
stop it from being corroded during transit.
All things considered, Kasdan had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:15.120
doing pretty well, given the circumstances.
That was until he heard the blare of alarms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.080
ringing out. His heart, which had already been&nbsp;
drumming away in his chest through sheer nerves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:26.560
now began beating so fast it threatened to crack&nbsp;
his ribs. Panic shot through his entire system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.840
and at that moment, all sense of rationality&nbsp;
was dropped faster than a lead balloon.&nbsp;

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.040
Any further attempts at subterfuge were pointless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.280
why keep hiding? Surely the alarms were for him,&nbsp;
Kasdan thought, and immediately started running,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.160
losing all cover. He barged past a pair&nbsp;
of Foundation researchers in lab coats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.160
knocking them both to the ground; a storm&nbsp;
of paper files that they’d been carrying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:56.240
were hurled up into the air, a temporary&nbsp;
smokescreen to cover Kasdan’s panicked escape.&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.960
One foot launching past the other, he barrelled&nbsp;
down the facility’s corridors, the same way he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.000
come in. If he was quick, he might make it&nbsp;
before they sealed the exits and trapped him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:12.240
inside. The chances were slim, and Kasdan knew it,&nbsp;
but he was left with no other choice apart from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.600
letting the SCP Foundation catch him, hauling&nbsp;
him off to God-knows-where for interrogation.&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.520
He barrelled past more Foundation staff,&nbsp;
some of them holding their hands out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:26.720
try and stop him as they figured out what the&nbsp;
alarms were for and why Kasdan was running.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:32.160
Shoving one out of the way, he felt something&nbsp;
snag at the lab coat he’d worn as a disguise.&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.800
One of the researchers had him!
Kicking a leg back, Kasdan clipped the man’s knee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.760
and whipped himself free of the coat, not letting&nbsp;
them stop him from running. He was close now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.600
so close to the door he’d come in through; if he&nbsp;
could just pass this corner, he’d be home free.&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.360
The clomp of multiple heavy, steel-toed&nbsp;
tactical boots came rushing through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.240
entrance to meet him. A squad of men – one&nbsp;
of the Foundation’s infamous Mobile Task&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:01.840
Forces – were hurtling towards Kasdan like&nbsp;
a tidal wave wearing all-black combat gear.&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:07.120
He skidded as he tried to turn back the way he’d&nbsp;
come, stumbling over his feet as he was chased by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:12.480
the sound of angry shouts commanding him to&nbsp;
freeze, drop the bag and get on the ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.200
Kasdan dared not look over his shoulder,&nbsp;
catching hints of the oncoming MTF agents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:22.320
in his peripheral vision, compelling him to&nbsp;
keep running. But with no idea where to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:28.080
and four heavily-armed operatives clipping at&nbsp;
his heels, there was little hope of escaping now.&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.200
A powerful, weighty force struck Kasdan’s back,&nbsp;
knocking the air out of his lungs as it pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:38.480
him over and kept him pinned to the floor. He&nbsp;
could barely move as the agent tackled him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:43.520
gasping as he desperately tried to pull his breath&nbsp;
back. The rest of the squad gathered around him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.360
all yelling and warning him not to&nbsp;
move. But there was another sound…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:53.920
no, another voice, drowning out the soldiers.&nbsp;
The earpiece, the one thing keeping his mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.920 --> 00:05:00.960
safe. It was gone, it must’ve fallen out when he&nbsp;
hit the ground… and now, the mask could get in.&nbsp;

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:06.160
The whispering was unintelligible, nonsense&nbsp;
really; Kasdan couldn’t clearly make out what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:12.640
it was saying. He only knew it had quickly become&nbsp;
the only thing he could hear, and how it made him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:19.120
feel. He had to put the mask on. It was such a&nbsp;
strong compulsion, it felt like so much more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:26.320
a want, a desire to wear it; it was a need.
The bag was so close, dropped to the floor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:31.280
when he had been tackled. If he could&nbsp;
just reach it and tear the zipper open,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.760
he’d have the mask in his hands.
Rolling over, Kasdan lashed out at the MTF&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:41.360
operative, catching him by surprise as his fist&nbsp;
connected with the man’s balaclava-covered face.&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.680
The agent was stunned, lifting some of his&nbsp;
weight that had been pinning the thief down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:50.160
just enough for Kasdan to free his other&nbsp;
hand. Another pair of agents tried to hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.360
his flailing arms to the ground, only for him to&nbsp;
reach up and pull one of them face-first into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:00.720
concrete floor with a bloody crunch. With every&nbsp;
ounce of strength that he could muster, Kasdan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.640
moved like a man possessed, hurling the agent on&nbsp;
his other arm into the first who had tackled him.&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.000
Slipping out from underneath the crumpled agents,&nbsp;
he crawled on his stomach as far and as fast as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:18.880
could. Kasdan desperately scrabbled for the duffel&nbsp;
bag. It was so close, a mere few inches away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.040
his fingertips brushing up against it&nbsp;
as he reached. But he couldn’t grab it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:28.640
as much as he felt that overwhelming need to. His&nbsp;
feet were still buried under the weight of the MTF&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:34.160
operators and their gear, stopping him from&nbsp;
reaching any further… until one of the agents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.920
moved, just enough to free Kasdan’s foot.
Everything seemed to move in slow motion. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.360
MTF soldiers were reaching out to pull Kasdan off&nbsp;
the floor, as his hands shot forward and tightly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.400
gripped the straps of his bag. He could feel hands&nbsp;
wrapped in tactical gloves gripping at his shirt;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.760
in the same instant, he wrenched the bag towards&nbsp;
him and pulled down the zipper. He had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:01.040
get to what was inside, even if it killed him.
He barely noticed his earpiece getting crunched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:06.400
under the heavy combat boot of one of the agents.&nbsp;
Instead, he was inhaling fumes from the interior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.840
of the bag, its specialized inner lining already&nbsp;
melting thanks to the viscous black substance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:16.640
secreting from the mask. Kasdan didn’t even&nbsp;
register the pain in his hands when he reached&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:22.080
inside, the secretion corroding his bare skin&nbsp;
as he retrieved what he’d been hired to steal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:29.680
what he now so desperately needed to put&nbsp;
on his face: SCP-035, the Possessive Mask.&nbsp;

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:35.120
Time felt like it had ground to a halt, freezing&nbsp;
everyone. Kasdan stared for a split second at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.000
the white porcelain surface of the mask. It&nbsp;
felt like it was glaring hatefully at him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:45.840
thanks to its exaggerated tragedy grimace.&nbsp;
It was almost as if it disproved of Kasdan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:51.440
as if he was somehow unworthy of it. But&nbsp;
holding it in his hands, the compulsion to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:58.320
put on SCP-035 was now so unbearable. Oblivious to&nbsp;
the Foundation agents around him, who were trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:04.640
in vain to restrain him again, Kasdan tipped his&nbsp;
face into the mask… and everything went black.&nbsp;

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:09.040
It was like being half asleep, his&nbsp;
awareness of certain things stripped away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:15.840
Things like the pain searing his face, a gradual,&nbsp;
acidic burning that was eating away at his flesh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.600
corroding his body. And yet, Kasdan could still&nbsp;
feel occasional sensations. Tremors running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.800
up his arms as his fists made contact with&nbsp;
something, then pulled back and struck again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:32.240
leaving behind something wet on his knuckles.&nbsp;
But he couldn’t see, all around him was shrouded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:38.000
in darkness. He knew his body was moving,&nbsp;
maybe even walking, taking him somewhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:45.440
but he had no clue where, and no control anymore.&nbsp;
It was like someone… something else had pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.880
his mind out of the driver’s seat, and now&nbsp;
had both its corruptive hands on the wheel.&nbsp;

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.120
His mind was lost in the&nbsp;
blackness. Shut down. Gone.&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.560
It was only when he came back around that Kasdan&nbsp;
felt the sheer, unrelenting agony fully wash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.840
over him. The mask was off again, leaving him a&nbsp;
scorched, screaming mess. He was laying on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:12.160
floor of another containment cell. This one was&nbsp;
different from the one he’d stolen SCP-035 from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:18.160
it was less heavily guarded, minimal security.&nbsp;
It might not even have been in the same facility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:22.320
Kasdan had no idea how long he’d been&nbsp;
wearing the mask for. All he knew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.960
apart from the intense pain of the corrosive&nbsp;
black sludge breaking his body down, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:33.440
bloodstains on his hands and clothes, was that he&nbsp;
wasn’t alone… someone else was in there with him.&nbsp;

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:39.920
Kasdan didn’t know the strangest part of all&nbsp;
this. He should be dead; No, he was dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:45.920
Much like Dr. Bright’s medallion, the Possessive&nbsp;
Mask typically wipes the human mind like Oxiclean.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:52.880
If he was back, it meant somebody brought&nbsp;
him back. Somebody with truly great power…&nbsp;

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:57.600
Craning his head up, he caught sight of the&nbsp;
cell’s only other occupant. Even squinting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:02.560
through his stinging eyes, Kasdan couldn’t&nbsp;
make out exactly where the other man was from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.360
only that he was much older. He was looking&nbsp;
down at Kasdan writhing on the floor;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:13.680
there was something almost… sad lingering in his&nbsp;
eyes. There was a kind of sympathy behind them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:19.520
not just from looking at someone with such&nbsp;
severe injuries, but an almost apologetic gaze,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:23.280
like he was sorry that the pain&nbsp;
even existed in the first place.&nbsp;

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:29.200
“Glad to see you’re back, my son,” the old&nbsp;
man said. “It’s been a while since I’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:34.640
needed to pull someone back from that deep in the&nbsp;
darkness. I was worried I’d be a little rusty…”&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:42.000
The old man gently reached a hand out towards him…&nbsp;
and took Kasdan’s pain away. He didn’t heal him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:47.680
not fully, just hit ‘pause’ on his wounds.&nbsp;
But before he could thank the kind stranger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:53.520
the mask started whispering again. Only&nbsp;
this time, it was calling to the old man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:59.600
No longer hurting but still reeling from what&nbsp;
SCP-035 had done to him, Kasdan tried to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:05.920
the man, calling with a rasping voice, begging&nbsp;
him not to listen to the Possessive Mask’s call.&nbsp;

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.880
He didn’t seem as spellbound as Kasdan had&nbsp;
been, in fact, the old man almost just looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:16.720
like he was going through the motions. Pacing&nbsp;
over to where SCP-035 lay on the cell floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:22.320
picking it up and, just like Kasdan had done,&nbsp;
he lifted the porcelain mask over his wrinkled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:27.440
wizened face. Helpless, unable to do&nbsp;
anything other than watch on in horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:33.840
Kasdan couldn’t help but notice the tragic frown&nbsp;
carved onto the surface of SCP-035 had shifted;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:41.120
now, it was a wide, gaping smile, a comedic&nbsp;
grin with nothing but ill intent behind it.&nbsp;

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:46.080
While he had no idea who the old man was,&nbsp;
some swirling, sickening feeling in the pit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.960
of Kasdan’s stomach told him nothing good could&nbsp;
come from putting that twisted mask over another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:57.040
anomalous being. If he had only known that&nbsp;
SCP-343 was colloquially nicknamed ‘God’ by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:02.240
the Foundation’s staff, and was widely believed&nbsp;
to be the sole creator of the entire universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:07.360
then Kasdan would have used all his strength&nbsp;
to pull the mask off the old man’s face and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:13.200
smash it to pieces. But it was already too late.
The very second the Possessive Mask slipped over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:19.520
SCP-343’s face, the ground shook violently,&nbsp;
like the very Earth itself was afraid of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:25.360
had just happened. Still watching from the cell&nbsp;
floor, Kasdan looked at this combined creature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:29.280
It stood still for a moment,&nbsp;
slowly breathing through the mask,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:35.040
before it lifted its hands and appeared to&nbsp;
examine them. The comedy smile on SCP-035 made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:40.800
it seem like the mask itself was looking with&nbsp;
a warped sense of glee at its new host body.&nbsp;

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:44.800
More of the same black goo was being&nbsp;
secreted out from beneath the mask,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.840
drops of it were rolling off the old man’s&nbsp;
shoulders. They landed on the cell floor, melting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:55.200
tiny, burning holes as the substance dripped down&nbsp;
through the concrete and steel of the facility.&nbsp;

00:12:55.200 --> 00:13:00.720
His body being puppeteered by the mask on his&nbsp;
face, the old man wiped a smear of the sludge away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:06.880
with his hand, looking at it in his fingers. It&nbsp;
wasn’t melting him the same way it had to Kasdan;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:12.720
usually, the corrosive secretion that SCP-035&nbsp;
naturally produced proved to be its weakness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.640
melting the bodies of its human&nbsp;
hosts and eventually destroying them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:23.520
leaving the mask without a form to pilot. SCP-343,&nbsp;
on the other hand, was only humanoid in shape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:27.760
and far beyond any mortal being that&nbsp;
the Possessive Mask had ever enthralled.&nbsp;

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:34.560
The combined being, corruptive mask and omnipotent&nbsp;
god, raised its hands high, like a conductor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:40.320
before an orchestra. From the spot he lay in,&nbsp;
Kasdan watched in horror as every member of staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:45.520
in the facility was pulled up through the floor,&nbsp;
or dragged screaming through the walls, piping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:51.200
and brickwork tearing through them. This was a&nbsp;
minimum-security Foundation wing, far more relaxed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:57.920
with only a handful of staff and a light force of&nbsp;
guards. Still, to SCP-035, it didn’t matter how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:03.280
many there were. It was enough to make a start.
The wrinkly hands of its new host clenched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:07.920
sharply; the Foundation staff, all&nbsp;
suspended in mid-air, suddenly exploded.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:12.960
Each one of them, every researcher and&nbsp;
guard, erupted into a fireball, burning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:18.880
white-hot like heated metal, before fizzling out.
There was nothing left, no scraps of clothing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:25.200
no remains, they just… weren’t.
If it wanted to, SCP-035 would have thrown its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:30.720
head back and laughed maniacally. In some strange&nbsp;
way, Kasdan thought that might have been better.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:36.720
Instead, it was silent, the mask’s wide, soulless&nbsp;
grin conveying its twisted delight well enough.&nbsp;

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:41.120
It turned to face the wall, thick&nbsp;
layers of concrete standing between it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:48.080
and the outside world, and began stepping forward,&nbsp;
so completely casually that it was unnerving.&nbsp;

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:54.880
With the first step, the walls of the cell&nbsp;
surrounding the SCP-035 and SCP-343 hybrid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.880 --> 00:15:00.960
as well as Kasdan, began to crumble away. With&nbsp;
the second, the corridor outside did the same,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:05.040
falling apart without any exertion&nbsp;
of effort from the masked god.&nbsp;

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:09.280
Each and every step further, more of the&nbsp;
building around them was chipped away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:13.440
carving a path through rooms and research&nbsp;
stations towards the edge of the site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:18.000
It was as though the concrete and brickwork,&nbsp;
the dense, heavy materials that constructed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:24.400
the facility suddenly had the consistency of&nbsp;
wet sand; and SCP-035 and its new host were the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:30.800
tides coming in, washing away all in their path.
No longer in pain, but his body distorted beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:36.480
repair, Kasdan forced himself up off the ground&nbsp;
at last. Weakly, he limped after the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:41.520
thinking in vain he had any chance to stand&nbsp;
against a being with the unbridled power of a god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:44.960
and the infinite cruelty and&nbsp;
malice of the Possessive Mask.&nbsp;

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:49.440
If he could just get close enough, Kasdan&nbsp;
thought, he could tear the mask away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:54.240
freeing the old man. He wouldn’t be able to&nbsp;
stop himself from putting it on a second time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:59.040
but perhaps it was better that Kasdan wore&nbsp;
it, and let its black ooze melt him down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:05.840
At least the wise, kindly old man would be able to&nbsp;
get far enough away from SCP-035’s influence, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:11.280
Kasdan could, at least in part, put this right.
After all, he’d stolen the mask from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:16.240
Foundation, this all started with him.
As the hybrid reached the farthest wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:20.800
the barrier turned to glass and shattered. The&nbsp;
combined monster looked out over the waiting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:27.600
helpless world. Through SCP-343, the Possessive&nbsp;
Mask had control over chaos and creation alike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:32.480
and nothing on Earth that could challenge&nbsp;
it. Not the Foundation, not humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:38.720
not even other anomalies. Lifting its still,&nbsp;
lifeless, grinning mask upwards, the sky darkened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:44.080
the deafening boom of thunder ringing out above.
Forked bolts of deep orange lightning cracked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:47.120
across the atmosphere, as what&nbsp;
was left of the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:52.000
facility dissolved behind the masked god.
Though it was facing out towards a world that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:58.000
would soon crumble as easily as this building, the&nbsp;
creature could see everything, far beyond where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:04.560
it stood, the lives of billions upon billions.
All at once, it watched plants grow while others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:10.800
wilted, animals born only to die, humans&nbsp;
living out their ritualistic existences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:17.200
each of them gradually heading for the same fate.&nbsp;
And through all of that, it saw a hand, trembling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:23.520
behind it, reaching for its mask: Kasdan.
He was so close, fingertips just about to brush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:30.400
the porcelain surface of SCP-035. When suddenly&nbsp;
the mask, and the old man wearing it, were gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:34.960
Kasdan turned around in confusion, only&nbsp;
to find it was now standing behind him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:39.840
It reached out one of the wrinkled, bony old&nbsp;
hands and touched a single finger on his forehead.&nbsp;

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:45.600
Kasdan blinked, and he was back. Back before the&nbsp;
heist, before any of the wanton devastation had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:50.080
begun. He recognized the room he was in,&nbsp;
and sat in the very same place where his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:56.000
mysterious benefactor had approached him with a&nbsp;
seemingly impossible job: to steal a mask from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:02.000
the SCP Foundation. Sure enough, sitting across&nbsp;
the table, obscured by shadow was the client.&nbsp;

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:07.840
But behind his eyes, Kasdan was trapped, helpless&nbsp;
as he watched himself live out the same events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:13.280
that had led to the mask being placed on the face&nbsp;
of God. He couldn’t change the course of history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:18.480
couldn’t avert the apocalypse that was&nbsp;
already happening. All he could do was watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:23.200
his heart sinking as his client pushed a&nbsp;
file across the table, opening it to reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:31.600
a photograph of his target, the thing he wanted&nbsp;
Kasdan to steal: SCP-035, the Possessive Mask.&nbsp;

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:38.720
And meanwhile, back in the new hell of its own&nbsp;
creation, the mask was having some real fun…&nbsp;

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:45.920
Now go and check out “SCP-035 THE POSSESSIVE&nbsp;
MASK” and “SCP-343 GOD” to learn even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:51.040
about this pair of anomalies, and pray that&nbsp;
nobody ever has the chance to combine them.

